\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Saviour, Thy dying love
\par Thou gavest me,
\par Nor should I aught withhold,
\par My Lord, from Thee;
\par In love my soul would bow,
\par My heart fulfil its vow,
\par Some offering bring Thee now,
\par Something for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. At the blest mercy-seat 
\par Pleading for me,
\par My feeble faith looks up,
\par Jesus, to Thee;
\par Help me to the cross to bear,
\par Thy wondrous love declare,
\par Some song to raise, or prayer-
\par Something for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Give me a faithful heart,
\par Likeness to Thee,
\par That each departing day
\par Henceforth may see
\par Some work of love begun,
\par Some deed of kindness done,
\par Some wanderer sought and won-
\par Something for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. All that I am and have,
\par Thy gifts so free,
\par In joy, in grief, through life,
\par O Lord for, for Thee.
\par And when Thy face I see, 
\par My ransomed soul shall be,
\par Through all eternity,  
\par Something for Thee. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

